===Verb===
{{en-verb|+!,++}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} To [[add]]; to subject to [[addition]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=ACER research series - Issues 93-95 |author=Australian Council for Educational Research |year=1973 |page=39 |passage=For him y is a unique number, like 7, but for the time being unknown — if one does the operation of ''''plussing''' 4' one still has, as a result, a unique number even though one does not yet know what it is. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Control of Human Behavior: Behavior modification in education |year=1974 |passage=The teacher observing the behavior of a child who is '''plussing''' or not-plussing is observing instances or not-instances of the concept of '''plussing'''. }}
# {{lb|en|often followed by 'up'}} To [[increase]] in [[magnitude]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=How to Create Comics: From Script to Print |author=Danny Fingeroth; Mike Manley |year=2006 |page=48 |ISBN=1893905608 |passage=I am doing a lot of writing here, '''plussing''' the script, adding sequences. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Direction and Viability of the Federal Protective Service |author=United States Congress House Committee on Homeland Security |year=2009 |passage=We are losing at the street level a number of officers, but we are '''plussing''' up deputy positions. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Military Retirement Reform |author=United States Congress House Committee on Armed Services Subcommittee on Military Personnel |year=2012 |page=24 |passage=And I believe that, if we can't recognize that in retirement, we ought to recognize it in '''plussing''' up hazardous duty pay, '''plussing''' up sea duty pay and all those other things that recognize people that don't punch out on Saturday, on Friday afternoon and go home, and just, you know, go day after day after day. }}
# To [[improve]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Strategies for Fast-Changing Times |author=Nate Booth |year=1998 |page=91 |ISBN=0761511342 |passage=Coach Wooden didn't have to depend upon having the most talented players on his team because he could depend upon '''plussing''' to constantly make everyone better. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Color Outside the Lines |author=Howard Hendricks |year=2007 |page=123 |ISBN=1418569720 |passage=Keep fooling around with it, improving it, and making it better. You know you have a unique factor when someone steals it. So keep the unique factor unique by constantly '''plussing''' it. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=How to Be Like Walt: Capturing the Disney Magic Every Day of Your Life |author=Pat Williams; Jim Denney |year=2004 |page=154 |ISBN=0757394469 |passage=He was a pioneer in '''plussing''' the artform of animated cartoons. He began by '''plussing''' Micky Mouse with sound, the '''plussing''' the Silly Symphonies with color. Walt '''plussed''' the skills of his artists by sending them to art school at his own expense. }}
# To provide [[critical]] [[feedback]] by giving [[suggestion]]s for [[improvement]] rather than [[criticism]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Myths of Creativity |author=David Burkus |year=2013 |ISBN=1118729889 |passage=The animators and directors on the receiving end of the plussing don't necessarily have to accept and incorporate the feedback, but '''plussing''' provides a method to share criticisms in a way that makes it more likely that they will. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Winning the Long Game: How Strategic Leaders Shape the Future |author=Steven Krupp; Paul J.H. Schoemaker |year=2014 |ISBN=1610394488 |passage=Strategic leaders can adapt the US Army's after-action review and Pixar's '''plussing''' technique (where you build on ideas rather than critique and subtract) to show their teams how to learn from mistakes. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Summary : Little Bets - Peter Sims |author=BusinessNews Publishing |year=2014 |page= |ISBN=2511022389 |passage=When people view the early drafts of ideas for their movies under development, they always use '''plussing''' to try and come up with suggestions for enhancements. Feedback is always given in an upbeat rather than a derogatory manner. }}
# {{lb|en|sales}} To sell [[additional]] [[related]] items with an original [[purchase]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Current Business Cyclopedia: Business Digest |year=1920 |passage=Good will is also secured by '''plussing''' the original purchase with another article that goes appropriately with it. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=How to Set Up and Operate Your Own Law Practice |author=Max Fallek |year=1986 |passage='''Plussing''' the original sale creates a win-win situation. The customer benefits because it often saves him the time necessary to run back to the store for overlooked items. }}
# {{lb|en|psychology}} To [[frame]] in a [[positive]] light; to provide a [[sympathetic]] [[interpretation]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Helping People in Crisis |author=Douglas A. Puryear |year=1979 |page=87 |passage='''Plussing''' is a technique for enhancing a positive atmosphere in the session, for diminishing hostility, and for raising self-esteem. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Planned short-term psychotherapy: a clinical handbook |author=Bernard L. Bloom |year=1997 |page=187 |passage=In addition to active listening as a general therapeutic strategy, Puryear identifies two specific techniques, '''plussing''' and paradox, that are used throughout the crisis intervention. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Crisis Intervention |author=Kenneth France |year=2015 |page=177 |ISBN=0398081077 |passage=When '''plussing''', the intervenor introduces novel viewpoints that can increase the self-esteem of both the attacker and the target. }}
# {{lb|en|social media|dated}} To give a mark of [[approval]] on {{w|Google+}}.
#: {{cot|en|like}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Optimize |author=Lee Odden |year=2012 |page=111 |ISBN=1118239571 |passage=How do you get others to add you or your brand to their circles? By creating and sharing useful content, commenting, '''plussing''' others' content and comments, and engaging with others on Google+. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Creativity, Inc. |author=Ed Catmull |year=2014 |page=279 |ISBN=1448126282 |passage=Everyone was '''plussing''' them or liking them or pinning them. The videos went viral. }}
# {{lb|en|homeopathy}} To [[increase]] the [[potency]] of a [[remedy]] by [[diluting]] it in [[water]] and [[stirring]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Transmission of Homoeo Drug Energy from Distance |author=B. Sahni |year=2005 |page=188 |ISBN=8170211352 |passage=On hearing this, '''plussing''' was done (all medicated water of the phial was thrown away and fresh distilled was added and 10 strokes were given) on the 13th February 1974. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Vaccine Free Prevention and Treatment of Infectious Contagious Disease with Homeopathy |author=Kate Birch |year=2007 |ISBN=1425118690 |passage=From the remaining water a second dilution can be prepared '''plussing''' it to the next slightly higher potency. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Homeopathy for Home: Acute Illness & Injury Care |author=Kim Lane |year=2011 |page=29 |ISBN=1465356797 |passage='''Plussing''' is used quite frequently in a patient who's quite sensitive or has an acute problem happening or needs to change his dose or need to take it over several days. }}
# {{lb|en|optometry}} To [[increase]] a [[correction]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The intraocular lens in perspective |author=David M. Worthen; Perry S. Binder |year=1976 |page=2 |ISBN=088372040X |passage=No aspheric cataract spectacle lens designer has ever given the slightest thought to this 4 to 6 diopters of over-'''plussing''' for peripheral vision which is responsible for tremendous peripheral distortion, worse peripheral swim, worse false orientation, worse magnification, severe concave curvature of field ("The floor comes up at you"), increased ring scotoma size and increase jack-in-the-box phenomenon (the "horse-blinder effect") with unsafe walking and driving. }}

